WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.849
CSV, JSON, Excel and Parquet: converting data without losing it.

2
00:00:07.349 --> 00:00:12.211
What each data format can and cannot hold, where conversions quietly break,

3
00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:15.712
and the tools I use to move data between them locally.

4
00:00:17.941 --> 00:00:23.665
Four formats, four ideas. Comma separated values is the oldest and simplest:

5
00:00:23.665 --> 00:00:26.602
one line per row, commas between cells.

6
00:00:28.731 --> 00:00:31.761
Try a conversion. Edit the CSV on the left.

7
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:39.197
Where conversions go wrong. JSON to CSV only works cleanly when every record

8
00:00:39.197 --> 00:00:40.524
has the same shape.

9
00:00:42.653 --> 00:00:46.150
To try it, open Data Format Converter in OpenFile.

10
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:50.137
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

11
00:00:50.137 --> 00:00:53.704
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

12
00:00:55.753 --> 00:00:59.700
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
